From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Schmiedel <Martin.Schmiedel@tq-group.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:12:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: freescale: fsl-samsung-hdmi: fix deadlock with
 clk_prepare_lock

A hdmi_pclk rate change holds clk_prepare_lock and resumes the PHY
through clk_pm_runtime_get(). The PHY runtime suspend calls
clk_disable_unprepare() and also takes clk_prepare_lock. If the suspend
runs at the same time, both tasks wait for each other.

Seen on i.MX8MP on a HDMI mode change (1080p60 <-> 1080p23.976):

  modetest: clk_set_rate() <- lcdif_crtc_atomic_enable()
            clk_core_set_rate_nolock() -> clk_pm_runtime_get() -> rpm_resume()
  kworker (pm_runtime_work): fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy_suspend()
            -> clk_unprepare() -> clk_prepare_lock()

All other clk users then block too (cpufreq, SDHCI runtime resume).

Keep apbclk prepared from probe and only gate it in runtime PM.
clk_enable() and clk_disable() do not take clk_prepare_lock.

Signed-off-by: Martin Schmiedel <Martin.Schmiedel@tq-group.com>
---
 drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c
index 0f25d81..d6110c1 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c
@@ -694,7 +694,11 @@ static int __maybe_unused fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy *phy = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	clk_disable_unprepare(phy->apbclk);
+	/*
+	 * clk_disable() only: runtime suspend can run while a hdmi_pclk rate
+	 * change holds clk_prepare_lock and waits in clk_pm_runtime_get().
+	 */
+	clk_disable(phy->apbclk);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -704,7 +708,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy_resume(struct device *dev)
 	struct fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy *phy = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	ret = clk_prepare_enable(phy->apbclk);
+	ret = clk_enable(phy->apbclk);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(phy->dev, "failed to enable apbclk\n");
 		return ret;
